worked_examples.problem:
What is printed by:
int f(int n) {
  static int r = 0;
  if (n <= 0) return 1;
  if (n > 3) { r = n; return f(n - 2) + 2; }
  return f(n - 1) + r;
}
int main() { printf("%d", f(5)); }

solved_examples.question:
What is the output of the following C code?
int a[] = {10, 20, 30, 40};
int *p = a;
printf("%d", *(p++) + *++p);

pyqs.text:
Consider the recursive C function:
int f(int n) {
  if (n <= 1) return 1;
  return f(n - 1) + f(n - 2);
}
What is the total number of calls to f when executing f(5)?

Consider code:
int a[] = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10};
int *p = a + 1;
What is the value of *(p + 2)?

How many times will 'Hello' be printed by the following code?
